## Context

`Tag:` was chosen over `Label:` for historical reasons unrelated to erg's design. The research
(2026-05-30) confirmed there is no open standard — the `labels` convention comes from GitHub and
GitLab, who use it to avoid collision with `git tag` (a versioning construct). erg has no git-tag
collision problem, but `labels` is the dominant convention and erg's controlled-vocabulary model
is semantically closer to "labels" (curated set, project-managed) than to "tags" (folksonomy,
free-form). Renaming removes gratuitous divergence with no functional cost.

The rename is cosmetic for agents — arrays of strings, same structure, same semantics. The
migration burden is real: spec, source, config, tests, docs, and existing ticket stores all say
`Tag:`. The `erg migrate` command is the right vehicle for corpus migration.

Scope confirmed:
- `src/go/assets/spec-erg-v1.md` — `Tag:` header, `[tags]` config section, `erg tag`/`untag` commands
- `src/go/assets/.ergrc` — `[tags]` section header and comment
- `src/go/erg.go`, `ergspecv1.go` — `Tags []string` field, `"Tag"` in allowed-header set
- `src/go/tag.go` — file likely renamed or repurposed; `cmdTag`/`cmdUntag`
- `src/go/list.go`, `main.go`, `migrate.go`, `validate.go`, `config.go` — all `tag`/`Tag` references
- `src/go/assets/integration.md` — integration notes mentioning tags
- `pep-erg-v1.md` — section 12 ("Tag header") title and body
- `docs/erg-manual.md` — all `tag`/`Tag`/`[tags]` references
- `tests/test_tag.sh`, `test_list.sh`, `test_ready.sh`, `test_validate.sh`, and all other test fixtures
- All `*_test.go` files using `Tag:` headers in fixture content

## Part 1 — Spec and PEP

- `src/go/assets/spec-erg-v1.md`: rename `Tag:` header to `Label:`, `.ergrc [tags]` to `[labels]`,
  commands `erg tag`/`erg untag` to `erg label`/`erg unlabel`
- Sync `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md` (the committed copy)
- `pep-erg-v1.md` section 12: rename "Tag header" to "Label header", update body

## Part 2 — Source

- `src/go/ergspecv1.go`: rename `Tags []string` field to `Labels []string`; add `"Label"` to
  allowed-header set; the old `"Tags:"` → `"Tag:"` migration hint becomes `"Tag:"` → `"Label:"`
- `src/go/erg.go`: parser case `"Tag"` → `"Label"`; `Tags:` legacy hint → `Tag:` legacy hint
- `src/go/tag.go`: rename file to `label.go`; rename `cmdTag` → `cmdLabel`, `cmdUntag` → `cmdUnlabel`
- `src/go/main.go`: update dispatch table (`tag` → `label`, `untag` → `unlabel`). HARD RENAME —
  no aliases. `erg tag`/`erg untag` become unknown commands, matching how Status→Closed and
  Tags→Tag landed (no codebase precedent for deprecated aliases).
- `src/go/list.go`: `Tags` field in JSON output → `labels`; filter argument help text
- `src/go/config.go` or equivalent: `[tags]` config key → `[labels]`
- `src/go/migrate.go`: add migration case `Tag:` → `Label:` (same pattern as existing `Tags:` → `Tag:`)

## Part 3 — `erg migrate` corpus migration

Add a new migration pass to `erg migrate`:

```
Tag: → Label: rewrite: N tickets
```

- Rewrite every `Tag:` header to `Label:` in preamble
- Rewrite `.ergrc` `[tags]` section header to `[labels]`
- Idempotent: a corpus already using `Label:` is a no-op
- Report counts as with existing migration passes

## Part 4 — Tests and docs

- `tests/test_tag.sh` → `tests/test_label.sh` (rename file; update all internal references)
- All test fixtures using `Tag:` headers → `Label:`
- `*_test.go` fixture strings: `Tag:` → `Label:`, `Tags []string` → `Labels []string`
- `docs/erg-manual.md`: all `tag`/`Tag`/`[tags]` → `label`/`Label`/`[labels]`
- `src/go/assets/integration.md`: update tag references

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `spec-erg-v1.md` uses `Label:` header, `[labels]` config, `erg label`/`erg unlabel` commands
- [ ] `pep-erg-v1.md` section 12 updated
- [ ] All Go source uses `Labels []string`, `"Label"` header key, `cmdLabel`/`cmdUnlabel`
- [ ] `erg tag`/`erg untag` removed (hard rename, no aliases); old `Tag:` header rejected with a
      `run erg migrate` hint
- [ ] `erg migrate` rewrites `Tag:` → `Label:` corpus-wide, idempotent (legacy `Tags:` converges
      to `Label:` in one run)
- [ ] `erg migrate` rewrites `.ergrc [tags]` → `[labels]`
- [ ] All test suites updated (`test_label.sh` replaces `test_tag.sh`)
- [ ] Repo corpus migrated: `tickets/*.erg` use `Label:`; `erg check tickets/` passes
- [ ] `make test` and `make validate` pass (the actual gates; there is no `make check` target)

## Notes

Hard rename, no dual-read window. `erg migrate` rewrites the `.ergrc` `[tags]` section text-level
(no `loadConfig()` dependency), so the source rename and config-key rename land in the same commit
— the sequencing concern in the original draft does not apply.

Landing hazard: the pre-commit hook validates staged `.erg` files with the committed (old)
`tickets/erg`, which rejects `Label:`. Commit the migrated corpus with `--no-verify`; CI rebuilds
`tickets/erg` after merge, closing the window.
